(4704678, 675427, 811, '<td valign="top">CRITIQUE CLUB CRITIQUE<br/>by karmat<br/> <br/>Compositionally, I think what you have done works fairly well.  It feels just a touch tight on the right and left though, and I was wondering what it might look like if it were a bit wider.  It is a cool effect, and I think you could probably get several different crops that all work out of it.  <br/> <br/>Technically, it is exposed well and the colors are nice.  I also like that the texture is visible in the shot.<br/> <br/>All of that said, technically, it was a nicely done shot.  However, the "illusion" just wasn''t strong enough to make it terribly interesting or compelling, and I think that shows in your score.<br/> <br/></td>', 'CRITIQUE CLUB CRITIQUEby karmat Compositionally, I think what you have done works fairly well.  It feels just a touch tight on the right and left though, and I was wondering what it might look like if it were a bit wider.  It is a cool effect, and I think you could probably get several different crops that all work out of it.   Technically, it is exposed well and the colors are nice.  I also like that the texture is visible in the shot. All of that said, technically, it was a nicely done shot.  However, the "illusion" just wasn''t strong enough to make it terribly interesting or compelling, and I think that shows in your score. ', '2008-05-15 15:26:56.000000', NULL, 0),
(4704803, 675731, 22180, '<td valign="top">Thanks for all comments.<br/>It was behind the glass and I had no choice to change the background color :)</td>', 'Thanks for all comments.It was behind the glass and I had no choice to change the background color :)', '2008-05-15 16:56:33.000000', NULL, 0),
(4704911, 676381, 79847, '<td valign="top">Thank you to everyone for leaving such great comments.  I''ve only submitted a few photos before this and really am a complete beginner.  This photo was taken, ''doing a dp cardinal sin'' and using the digital zoom on my camera, which is why it''s not the crisp photo it could be.  I found it much easier to get the right composition this way.  <br/> <br/>I was excited when I saw the triangular composition because it''s a perfect catagory for Mt Taranaki photos.  It had been very cold and snowing up the mountain till the morning this was taken.  The clouds soon grew and again covered us in cold miserable weather, so I was lucky to get this shot when I did.<br/> <br/>I take lots of photos, of the mountain, because I only have to venture to the deck to take them and it''s such a beautiful scenery.  I haven''t yet taken a photo that I''m completely satisfied with (does that ever happen - lol), but when I do I''m going to print it to canvas for the wall in the lounge.<br/> <br/>Thanks again<br/>Maryanne</td>', 'Thank you to everyone for leaving such great comments.  I''ve only submitted a few photos before this and really am a complete beginner.  This photo was taken, ''doing a dp cardinal sin'' and using the digital zoom on my camera, which is why it''s not the crisp photo it could be.  I found it much easier to get the right composition this way.   I was excited when I saw the triangular composition because it''s a perfect catagory for Mt Taranaki photos.  It had been very cold and snowing up the mountain till the morning this was taken.  The clouds soon grew and again covered us in cold miserable weather, so I was lucky to get this shot when I did. I take lots of photos, of the mountain, because I only have to venture to the deck to take them and it''s such a beautiful scenery.  I haven''t yet taken a photo that I''m completely satisfied with (does that ever happen - lol), but when I do I''m going to print it to canvas for the wall in the lounge. Thanks againMaryanne', '2008-05-15 17:44:31.000000', NULL, 0),
